    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This distinctive 1930s Art Deco three-bedroom home is presented in excellent condition throughout, combining the character and strong architectural lines of its era with a bright, stylish and very well-maintained interior. Extending to approximately 132.4 sq. m. excluding the garage, the house offers generous and practical family accommodation, two bathrooms, a separate utility room, integral garage and excellent off-street parking.\r\n\r\nThe house has particularly good kerb appeal and is set well back from the road, approached by a generous driveway providing ample off-street parking. Mature boundaries provide a good degree of privacy, while the distinctive flat-roofed façade and clean lines retain the unmistakable Art Deco character of the original house.\r\n\r\nInside, the excellent standard of presentation is immediately apparent. The accommodation is bright, comfortable and ready for immediate occupation, with a layout that works particularly well for modern family living.\r\n\r\nThe two reception rooms are currently open to one another in an attractive open-plan arrangement, creating a generous and flexible living space. The front reception provides a comfortable main sitting area, while the second reception to the rear works naturally as an additional family or entertaining space and has direct access to the garden. Together, they provide a great sense of space while retaining the proportions and character of the original rooms.\r\n\r\nThe large kitchen/dining room, measuring approximately 7.25m x 5.41m, is another standout feature. Generously proportioned and very well presented, it provides plenty of room for cooking, dining and everyday family life, with direct access outside. A separate utility room keeps the practical side of the house neatly away from the main living areas, while the ground-floor shower room is a further useful addition. The integral garage provides excellent additional storage.\r\n\r\nUpstairs there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, including two particularly generous double bedrooms, together with the main family bathroom. Combined with the shower room downstairs, the property benefits from the convenience of two bathrooms.\r\n\r\nThe location is excellent, with Raheny Village and Raheny DART Station within easy reach, providing a great selection of shops, cafés and services together with regular connections to the city centre. The area is also very well served by Dublin Bus routes, making commuting particularly straightforward.\r\n\r\nSome of Dublin’s best outdoor amenities are close at hand. St Anne’s Park, the seafront, Dollymount Strand and Bull Island provide an exceptional choice of parkland, coastal walks, cycling routes and sporting facilities. There is also an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools, sports clubs and recreational amenities throughout Raheny, Clontarf and Killester.\r\n\r\nWith its distinctive Art Deco architecture, excellent presentation, generous accommodation and substantial set-back from the road, this is a particularly appealing family home that has been very well cared for and is ready for its next owners to enjoy."
      },
